# PR Review Slack Message Format

## When to Use

Trigger when user requests: "gerar comentário de PR", "PR review para QA", "comentário para slack", "review QA"

## Required Format

```
#PR Review: [Título descritivo e conciso] ([link da PR se disponível])
Ticket: [Contexto do ticket] → [Item específico] ([link Slack se disponível])

[Categoria] :emoji: — [Descrição de 1 linha: mudança + impacto]
[Categoria] :emoji: — [Descrição de 1 linha: mudança + impacto]
[Categoria] :emoji: — [Descrição de 1 linha: mudança + impacto]
Dev: @Vitor
QA: @Concli — [instruções específicas de teste]
```

**Notes:**
- Ticket line is optional (include when there's a Slack thread or ticket link)
- Use Slack emoji syntax (`:white_check_mark:`, `:zap:`, `:lock:`, `:fire:`, `:bug:`)
- Dev defaults to `Vitor` unless explicitly specified otherwise
- QA defaults to `Concli` unless explicitly specified otherwise

## Best Practices

- Maximum 5-6 items, 1 line each
- No blank lines between items (Slack formatting)
- Focus on QA-relevant changes, not implementation details
- Use emojis sparingly for emphasis
- Highlight priorities and critical items
- Include PR link when available

## Emoji Guide

- `:white_check_mark:` New feature
- `:zap:` Enhancement / UX improvement
- `:lock:` Security / permissions
- `:fire:` Significant performance improvement (>50%)
- `:bug:` Important bugfix
- `:warning:` Breaking change or special attention
- `:card_file_box:` SQL migration

## Analysis Process

1. Analyze all changes in the branch (all commits from main, not just latest)
2. Identify main features/fixes, group related changes
3. Prioritize for QA: what needs testing? what's user-facing? what's risky?
4. Structure as 5-6 items max, 1 line each
5. Add specific testing guidance in QA line

## Categories

- Filtros, Performance, UX/UI, Bugfix, API, Autenticação, Mensagens, Contatos, Funil, Agendamento, Uploads
